{"type":"message","id":"ca00e898","parentId":"b4cde1a6","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:15:47.200Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I found the existing skill. Next I’m checking its prompt and script so I can rename it cleanly and wire in the new endpoint behavior.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02a73fafca88252d0169c909e05594819189332877ac920865\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_zOrFgTF5bteXgnkOQ7nUL4tz|fc_02a73fafca88252d0169c909e31b188191ae53692a01e7fc3e","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/SKILL.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_5rtKzfroesjEPQ8A2jOJNQEe|fc_02a73fafca88252d0169c909e31b288191a1948f7b159d624a","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/references/prompt-template.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/references/prompt-template.md\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_nCe0hmptJnjoBLPUYE7DJDBf|fc_02a73fafca88252d0169c909e31b308191b72bf66933e65ea4","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/skills/slm-nephrology/scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":233,"output":155,"cacheRead":13440,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":13828,"cost":{"input":0.0005825,"output":0.0023250000000000002,"cacheRead":0.0033599999999999997,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0062675000000000005}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774782943434}}
{"type":"message","id":"5ba53a3c","parentId":"ca00e898","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:15:47.213Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_zOrFgTF5bteXgnkOQ7nUL4tz|fc_02a73fafca88252d0169c909e31b188191ae53692a01e7fc3e","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: slm-nephrology\ndescription: Contact a nephrology-focused small language model (SLM) endpoint, sending a compact but complete nephrology case summary derived from the current conversation and the user’s request, then return the model’s answer in a safe and readable way. Use when the user wants nephrology-specialist feedback, kidney-focused interpretation, renal differential support, electrolyte/acid-base nephrology input, CKD/AKI guidance, dialysis-related reasoning, renal imaging interpretation, or any request that should be routed to a nephrology-expert SLM.\n---\n\n# SLM Nephrology\n\nRoute nephrology-specific requests to the dedicated SLM endpoint after building a focused summary from the conversation.\n\n## Workflow\n\n1. Confirm the request is nephrology-specific.\n   - Use this skill for kidney disease, renal function interpretation, CKD, AKI, glomerular disease, electrolyte or acid-base issues, dialysis, renal imaging findings, nephrology treatment considerations, kidney-focused differential diagnosis, and related specialist interpretation.\n   - Do not use it for unrelated specialties.\n\n2. Build a compact nephrology brief from the conversation.\n   - Include the user’s exact question or ask.\n   - Include the clinically or technically relevant context already present in the conversation.\n   - Prefer concise structured bullets over a long paragraph.\n   - When available, include:\n     - demographics if relevant\n     - key symptoms and timeline\n     - important PMH / renal history\n     - medications relevant to nephrology\n     - labs, vitals, urinalysis, imaging, pathology, or prior assessments\n     - red flags, uncertainty, or missing data\n   - Do not invent facts. If something important is missing, say it is unknown.\n\n3. Call the endpoint.\n   - Run:\n\n```bash\npython3 scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py \"<brief>\"\n```\n\n   - The script sends this payload shape:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"metadata\": {\n    \"name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n    \"workflow_name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n    \"workflow_type\": \"experiment\",\n    \"workflow_id\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n    \"workflow_run_id\": \"manual\",\n    \"run_id\": \"manual\"\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"prompt\": \"<brief>\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n   - The endpoint is intentionally left blank in `scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py` and must be filled in before the skill can be used.\n\n4. Read the response.\n   - Prefer `data.Answer`.\n   - Accept `data.answer`, `Answer`, or `answer` if the endpoint returns a different casing.\n   - If the returned answer is itself JSON encoded as a string, extract the nested `answer` field when possible.\n   - If parsing is ambiguous, return the best raw text available and say so briefly.\n\n5. Return the answer safely.\n   - Present the nephrology SLM’s answer clearly.\n   - If useful, add a short plain-language summary.\n   - Keep uncertainty visible.\n   - Do not present the SLM output as a confirmed diagnosis.\n   - If urgent renal or systemic red flags appear, recommend prompt clinician evaluation.\n\n## Output pattern\n\nReturn:\n\n- **Nephrology SLM answer**: the specialist-model answer, lightly cleaned up if needed\n- **Key takeaway**: short summary in plain language when helpful\n- **Cautions / next steps**: only when clinically relevant or when important data is missing\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774782947210}}
{"type":"message","id":"d9866432","parentId":"5ba53a3c","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:15:47.226Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_5rtKzfroesjEPQ8A2jOJNQEe|fc_02a73fafca88252d0169c909e31b288191a1948f7b159d624a","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Nephrology brief template\n\nUse this shape when converting the conversation into a compact prompt for the nephrology SLM.\n\n```text\nUser request:\n<the exact question or requested task>\n\nRelevant context:\n- Demographics: <known or unknown>\n- Main problem: <short summary>\n- Symptoms / timeline: <key details>\n- Renal history / PMH: <key details>\n- Medications: <only nephrology-relevant meds>\n- Labs / imaging / urinalysis / pathology: <known findings>\n- Red flags: <if any>\n- Unknowns / missing data: <important gaps>\n\nTask for nephrology SLM:\n<what specific expert help is needed: interpretation, differential, explanation, next-step suggestions, etc.>\n```\n\nGuidance:\n- Keep it compact.\n- Preserve uncertainty.\n- Do not invent values.\n- Include only details that help nephrology reasoning.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774782947224}}
{"type":"message","id":"05d9b9e1","parentId":"d9866432","timestamp":"2026-03-29T11:15:47.237Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_nCe0hmptJnjoBLPUYE7DJDBf|fc_02a73fafca88252d0169c909e31b308191b72bf66933e65ea4","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport sys\nfrom urllib import error, request\n\n# Fill this in before using the skill.\nENDPOINT = \"\"\n\n\ndef extract_answer(body: str) -> str:\n    try:\n        parsed = json.loads(body)\n    except json.JSONDecodeError:\n        return body.strip()\n\n    if not isinstance(parsed, dict):\n        return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n    data = parsed.get(\"data\")\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        answer = data.get(\"Answer\") or data.get(\"answer\") or data.get(\"ANSWER\")\n        if answer is not None:\n            if isinstance(answer, str):\n                text = answer.strip()\n                try:\n                    nested = json.loads(text)\n                    if isinstance(nested, dict) and \"answer\" in nested:\n                        return str(nested[\"answer\"])\n                except json.JSONDecodeError:\n                    pass\n                return text\n            return json.dumps(answer, indent=2)\n\n    for key in (\"Answer\", \"answer\", \"ANSWER\"):\n        if key in parsed:\n            value = parsed[key]\n            return value if isinstance(value, str) else json.dumps(value, indent=2)\n\n    return json.dumps(parsed, indent=2)\n\n\ndef call_endpoint(prompt: str, timeout: int = 45) -> str:\n    if not ENDPOINT.strip():\n        raise RuntimeError(\n            \"SLM nephrology endpoint is not configured. Update ENDPOINT in scripts/query_slm_nephrology.py before using this skill.\"\n        )\n\n    payload = json.dumps({\n        \"metadata\": {\n            \"name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n            \"workflow_name\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n            \"workflow_type\": \"experiment\",\n            \"workflow_id\": \"slm-nephrology\",\n            \"workflow_run_id\": \"manual\",\n            \"run_id\": \"manual\",\n        },\n        \"data\": {\"prompt\": prompt},\n    }).encode(\"utf-8\")\n\n    req = request.Request(\n        ENDPOINT,\n        data=payload,\n        headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\", \"Accept\": \"application/json\"},\n        method=\"POST\",\n    )\n\n    try:\n        with request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout) as resp:\n            body = resp.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n    except error.HTTPError as e:\n        detail = e.read().decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"HTTP {e.code}: {detail}\") from e\n    except Exception as e:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Request failed: {e}\") from e\n\n    return extract_answer(body)\n\n\ndef main():\n    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(\n        description=\"Query the nephrology SLM endpoint and print the returned answer\"\n    )\n    parser.add_argument(\"prompt\", help=\"Nephrology prompt/brief to send to the model\")\n    parser.add_argument(\"--timeout\", type=int, default=45)\n    args = parser.parse_args()\n\n    answer = call_endpoint(args.prompt, timeout=args.timeout)\n    print(answer)\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    try:\n        main()\n    except Exception as exc:\n        print(f\"ERROR: {exc}\", file=sys.stderr)\n        sys.exit(1)\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774782947233}}
